{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/534613-halogen-stars-what-a-changeling-paris-game-should-have","id":534613,"title":"Halogen Stars-What a Changeling Paris Game Should Have","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-31T11:21:34-07:00","id":534613,"title":"Halogen Stars-What a Changeling Paris Game Should Have","content":"So, I've mentioned here and there I'm going to be running a Changeling game in Paris sometime soon. I have my own ideas, and I'm going to build predominantly off of the characters once I get them, but I figured hell, it worked for Az over in the Werewolf threads, let's do it here. So, borrowing his words, &quot;What should feature in a Paris [Changeling] chronicle? What are cool locations, interesting bits of culture and really cool elements of folklore and urban myth that should definitely be included? What are the obvious spiritual hotspots and centres of occult weirdness?&quot;<br /> <br /> PS: That entire Hedge discussion might happen next week, I've got stuff to do today. Blegh, never time. Still, I have started it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:17:46-07:00","id":534746,"title":"","content":"In Golden Eagle I plan to have Paris use a traditional Seasonal Court system, with the Spring Court having significant power. Essentially any time of year they are politically strong even if not the current monarch. I am having the Spring Court based in Pigalle, which is full of caberets, adult shops, and a lot more music shops and such than people generally associate with it. Of course, the Moulin Rouge is there. Full disclosure, though, it is touristy as hell.<br /> <br /> French posters know more than I, but from my visits I recall how much time I spent walking and stopping in various cafes and street restaurants. When I ran a Old WoD Changeling game there that was something I had PCs stopping at a lot. Perhaps it just reflects on me as a bumpkin in central North Carolina, but the endless amounts of fine restaurants and art museums really impressed me above and beyond other major European cities I visited, and it is second only to Vienna I think with my association with the music that played there. It had the best bread I have ever had. And my experiences with the locals I did not find them rude at all, despite having heard that several times. I'll try to think about more than just gushing about how awesome Paris is.<br /> <br /> The Paris sewers are rather infamous, and depending on how much crossover you tend to use may be a good location for the Autumn Court to be based, maybe even linking to it's own part of the Hedge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T13:34:56-07:00","id":534776,"title":"","content":"This is step one toward a big crossover.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also of note, while I have every reason to believe that Paris has Seasonal Courts today, I'm not going to be running with them for this game. I'm anticipating the Court Creation rules and making my own, fixing them as I receive information with everyone else. If my group is okay with it, I might even share the results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 05-31-2015, 07:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T16:36:45-07:00","id":534942,"title":"","content":"The Catacombs would be a definite spiritual hotspot/center of occult weirdness. I mean, a massive subterranean ossuary housing the remains of around 6 million people? Yeah, that might be a point of interest in a horror game. Between the Catacombs and the Sewers (which each have their own touristy museums, btw), there's a lot going on <i>under</i> Paris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5910-csschulz","name":"CSSchulz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5910_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T19:17:50-07:00","id":535025,"title":"","content":"I'm planning on introducing some friends to WoD with a hunter game set in Paris, so I'm very interested in what you'll come up with for changelings. Here are some observations :<br /> While we kind of lost it in the last 50 years, Paris was of very big in terms of arts, especially music. 90% of every famous composer active after 1750 stayed in either Vienna or Paris for an extensive period of time (yes, I'm pulling those numbers out of my ass, but you get the idea). Other artforms aren't really my domain of expertise, but I think it was pretty much the same deal. In the beginning of the 20th century, if you were an artist from Eastern Europe (or ironically the US), Paris was pretty much the place to go to make it in the West. There also was all that enlightment thing in the 17th century, so philosophy and litterature were pretty big.<br /> Also to note the political influence of the city, whether it was the royal family from the begining of the millenium to the 18th century. The whole Napoleonian military expansion of the 19th century. Or the complete clusterfuck that was the 20th century.<br /> So depending on how old you want your courts to be, and their nature (real government, focus on legislating the changeling population, or more of a society focused on other things) you could have decadent nobles, revolutionnary activists, groups that take the ideology of the resistance against the gentry (which is a TERRIBLE idea, but stupid people exist), or different regroupment of culturally minded people (see for example &quot;groupe des six&quot; or anyone that Cocteau ever touched), that can go from living a Dandy lifestyle in big appartments with a great view, to going from bar to bar to caf\u00e9 and crashing where they can.<br /> <br /> As for the locations :<br /> - the center of the city is the very touristic part, with Notre-Dame and all the museums (Louvres, Orsay...), l'\u00cele Saint-Louis (an island in the Seine), which is probably one of the richest places, &quot;les quais de Seine&quot;, i.e the docks where a bunch of people hang out and drink.<br /> -West of that you got the Champs de Mars, the Eiffel Tower and a few other touristic landmarks.<br /> -North of the center, you've got a distric comprised of the Op\u00e9ra Garnier (the one the phantom came from), les galeries Lafayette which is the chic market, and all the Hausmanian Boulevards (big fucking streets with the very caracteristic buildings), Champs Elys\u00e9es, Arc de Triomphe, and all that shit.<br /> <br /> -North of that is a poorer district, where we have Montmartre (which was huge for gipsy and factory workers culture in the beginning of the 20th century), le Sacr\u00e9-Coeur. It's also where most of the immigrants live.<br /> <br /> -East of the center is the Republique/Bastille district, which is extremely lively, lots of things happen there, meeting place for a lot of people, lots of cultural events.<br /> <br /> -South of Paris is a little less noteworthy, you've got most of the universities, lots of stores, bunch of people live there, so that would be the standard part town of the city. Note that this is where there is the touristic entrance to the catacombs (Denfer-Rocherau), but there are a lot of sealed entrances throughout the city. I'd see it more as a place that attracts a lot of thrill-seeking people which supernatural creatures actually avoid because that would be too clich\u00e9. The sewers would be my go to underground hiding place if I didn't want to be seen. Both are plenty spooky though.<br /> <br /> -Parts of suburbia to note : anything that takes place in corporate land is centered around La D\u00e9fense. Versailles, for the remnants of a once mighty nobility. All the towns centered around St Germain en Laye, for the very Bourgeois. St Denis is the very ghettoy area. Everything else is pretty much interchangeable standard town with varying degrees of standards of living.<br /> <br /> As for the folklore part, I'd suggest you read &quot;les contes de la rue Broca&quot;, it's for kids, but also modern fairy tales. Maupassant for the darker urban fantasy. And obviously Charles Perrault. Paris was actually rebuilt from the ground up in the 19th century, so there's not a lot of remnants from the fairy tales days in terms of places.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you have any questions, feel free.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6219-kzz","user":"kzz","date":". 05-31-2015, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6219-kzz","name":"kzz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T20:44:25-07:00","id":535157,"title":"","content":"When it comes to the courts, I'm creating them as a group rather than coming up with something and Arc-welding(heh) it into the world. That said, I imagine the new court came in sometime around after the 1890s. Were I making them myself, I would make the transition somewhere around 1946, with the French beginning to rebuild their sense of identity and pride alongside surrealism starting to pick up steam, and particularly using Cocteau's La Belle Et La Bete as a framework juxaposed to Perrault's Little Red Riding Hood and mixed in with the old swashbuckler ideals of the Sun Court. But it really depends on what the group brings to the table.<br /> <br /> As for the rest of this, this was the most useful breakdown of the city I've come across yet, so thanks a lot!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T01:00:56-07:00","id":535347,"title":"","content":"Also, don't forget the pretty large arabic/muslim/non-european population living in huge suburbs in Paris. An interesting movement I'd place there (with summer-courtiers and spring courtiers fighting for influence!) is the <a href=\"http://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/La_Rage_du_peuple\" target=\"_blank\">la rage du peuple </a>music collective. Sadly it is all in french and I barely know the language, but to understand the doctrine of the movement enjoy listening to a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=r1Co1mfz23U\" target=\"_blank\">music video (with subs)</a> made by the founder, Keny Arkana.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6030-a_newfie","name":"A_Newfie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"92"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T07:17:45-07:00","id":535547,"title":"","content":"Oh, believe me,I had not forgotten, though I did <i>not</i> know about the collective. That's super interesting.<br /> <br /> But yeah, Paris's large Muslim population is something I was totally going to do work with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T22:12:20-07:00","id":546499,"title":"","content":"You can't think of Paris without the oddity of the Eiffel tower, sure it isn't made of cold iron but perhaps the apartment up top is. If you want swashbucklers then the musketeers, changeling warriors sworn to protect the current monarch, whatever court he comes from. As for the Muslim population, don't forget that the foreigners among them bring their own myths and stories with them. Things like the Jinn, spirits that grant wishes that are more like bargains that rarely turn out the way you want, or ancient orders of assassins not too dissimilar to ninja, and ancient Persia has a mythology to equal anything out of Greece.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-08T22:32:42-07:00","id":546511,"title":"","content":"Ooh, I could do something like-but I dare not say.<br /> <br /> But all y'all, please, tell me more. MOAR!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}